WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:08.250
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:14.760
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.590
It's my day!

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.170
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.580
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.950
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:49.360
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.130
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.270
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.780
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.920
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.990
I just want to walk

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.530
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.500
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:35.400
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:41.840
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.110
It's my day!

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.290
Tsukushi Makino...

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.530
Rui Hanazawa...

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.640
I'll have these two expelled
within one week!

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.820
<i>Expelled?!</i>

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.660
I'll do whatever it takes to get rid of you.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.160
A-are you serious, Tsukasa?
This is Rui you're talking about!

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.960
Shut up, and mind your own business!

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.910
Just a...

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.880
Wait...

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.390
Just a minute!

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:01.790
Wait, I said!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.760
Why do we have to be expelled?

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:10.470
What gives you the right
to do this, Tsukasa?

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.040
<i>What?</i>

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.210
<i>Don't look at me like that.</i>

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.690
<i>Don't look at me as though...</i>

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.390
<i>...you can see right through me.</i>

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:53.240
"Love's Tempest! Being Expelled?!"

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.690
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.020
Well, I guess that's it.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:13.360
His family has always made
huge donations to Eitoku.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.760
If he threatens to cut off the donations...

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.070
...they'll cut us loose in a flash.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.120
Uh... Mom...

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.350
Oh, no! Another month in the red!

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.520
Dear, why haven't you gotten promoted?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.910
I-it can't be helped. Times are hard.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.260
It CAN be helped!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.900
Today, I heard Mrs. Tanaka gossiping.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.470
She said we're in over our heads,
sending Tsukushi to Eitoku.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:13.110
Er... uh... Actually, I'm going to be...

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:14.430
But!

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.810
When I told her Tsukushi was dating
the heir to Hanazawa Trading,

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.930
her jaw dropped!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.840
Even if we have to live on fumes,

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.990
we have to tighten our belts to send her
on to Eitoku University.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.600
Oh, Tsukushi...
Were you going to say something?

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.600
No, not really... Good night.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.850
<i>I can't tell them.</i>

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.860
<i>There's no way...</i>

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.880
<i>I'm going to be expelled...</i>

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.860
<i>I'll have these two expelled
within one week!</i>

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.490
<i>Well, I guess that's it.</i>

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.430
What do you mean, "that's it"?

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.880
Why do things like this
always happen to me?!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:05.870
What's going on?!

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.630
It's you who should be expelled!

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.520
Enough already. 
 I said I'd do it, and I will.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.020
But to do it by threatening to
cut off your parents' money...

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:18.780
Yeah...

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.080
We've had kids quit after
receiving a red slip from us,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.030
but the F4 has never had
anyone expelled.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.030
That's what was so cool about us.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.040
And to replace Rui...

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.130
with <i>this</i> guy, of all things?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.370
Don't try to act cool!

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.080
Tsukasa, we don't need
anyone to take Rui's place.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.540
He's been one of us 
since we were kids.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.010
Come on... forget this.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.830
I can't forgive him.
<i>Especially</i> because he's Rui.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.670
Do you think he really loves Makino?

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.390
I-I suppose he does...

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:12.260
The only girl he loves,
to this day, is Shizuka.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.070
Shizuka's about to get married.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:18.570
Rui's just using Makino to
try to forget everything.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.940
Tsukasa... you...

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.750
What's all this shouting about?

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.620
You're yammering like a bunch of kids!
What's going on?

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.650
Talk to him, will you, Tsubaki? He...

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.910
Akira! If you say
 anything, you'll be sorry.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.550
It's nothing. This has nothing
to do with you.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:57.110
Listen! Is that any way to
talk to your big sister?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.010
What's with this kid? He's frozen.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:00.880
Huh?

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.510
You mean Tsukushi's going
with Rui Hanazawa?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.020
Tsukushi and Rui Hanazawa?

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.620
Tsukushi and...?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.550
What's wrong with him?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.720
He's so depressing.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:23.360
This has cleared things up for me.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:24.670
For me, too.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.570
Tsukasa's really fallen
 for Tsukushi Makino.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:31.090
Yeah...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.060
But... I'm a little envious.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.170
I've never fallen so hard for one girl.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.210
Yeah... Rui's in big trouble.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.890
Yeah. He'll be expelled, for sure.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.570
Hey... where's the <i>nouveau riche</i>?

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.970
Forget about him.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.650
You'll tell me what's going on,

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.290
won't you?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.290
Hey, did you hear?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.020
It looks like Tsukushi Makino's finally
going to be expelled.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:33.760
Really?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.820
I'm surprised she lasted so long.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:40.470
No one's ever lasted a month after being
singled out by the F4.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:46.280
<i>Well, I'm delighted to be getting away
from those nitwits.</i>

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.180
Makino!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.090
Ugh! Sakurako!

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.720
I heard...

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:58.590
You're being expelled?

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:02.830
I'll be so lonely without you!

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.600
You're smiling...

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:08.250
Even if you're expelled and out of luck,

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.800
let's get together sometime.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:11.870
Yeah, right.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.790
Domyoji's gone to talk to the principal.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.690
Yeah?

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.140
I guess it's finally time for the execution.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:22.100
Principal's Office

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:22.100
<i>It's the end...</i>

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.100
D-Domyoji...

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.690
<i>Good-bye, Eitoku Academy...</i>

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.810
You want to stop the donations?

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:30.310
B-but...

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.910
<i>I guess it's time to say goodbye...</i>

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.620
<i>It's so full of bad memories.</i>

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:42.920
<i>But I did love that stairway.</i>

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.550
Won't you reconsider it?

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.770
<i>Goodbye...</i>

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.500
Say... That woman...

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.820
She's that legendary '82 grad...

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.280
Tsukasa Domyoji's sister...

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.880
It's Tsubaki Domyoji!

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.460
Tsukasa!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.630
Really? Tsubaki Domyoji is here?

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:29.750
But why? Isn't she in America?

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:33.300
Wow! I've always wanted to meet her!

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.610
<i>Why is Domyoji's sister here?</i>

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:41.240
How do you all know her?

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:44.620
As always, you're such a hick.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:48.100
Tsubaki Domyoji...

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:52.890
While she was in high school,
she was a model in Paris.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.850
She's extremely bright and
she's multi-lingual.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.500
And to top it all off...

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:01.270
She married a hotel magnate's heir
while in college.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:06.240
We idolize her even more
than we do Shizuka.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:08.820
And here at Eitoku Academy, she is...

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.210
...a legend!

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:15.680
I'm not sure if I get it,
but she seems to be quite a woman.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:20.150
It's a high-class thing.
You wouldn't understand.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:23.420
Don't touch her, Yuriko.
You'll get cooties.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.160
Hey, Yomogi!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:25.820
Huh?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.960
I'm glad you're here. Come with me.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:34.330
What?! She knows Makino?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.940
Um, Tsubaki... 
My name is "Tsukushi"...

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:44.800
Expel Rui Hanazawa and
Tsukushi Makino?

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.480
It's that simple.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:51.950
Expel them and we'll keep on donating.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:55.420
Makino might not be a problem,
but Hanazawa...

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:58.690
His father's very powerful...

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:02.030
It means nothing unless
they're expelled together!

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.010
Listen to me... You know that hall
you built with our money?

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.950
I could tear it all down.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.600
P-please...

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.560
So, what will it be?

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:14.970
Tsukasa!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.340
S-sis!

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.610
W-what? What are you doing?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:36.160
I'm absolutely mortified!
What kind of a coward are you?

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:40.090
Damn! Who told her?!

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.730
Sorry...

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:46.900
Kazuya! Damn you!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.740
In any case, sir, please disregard this.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.810
No way!

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.610
I want them out of here!

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:58.110
If you expel them, you'll be sorry!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.850
Keep out of this, Sis.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.350
What's that?!

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.950
I'll leave this school.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.760
You don't have to expel me.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.850
I'll quit.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.530
Are you satisfied?

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:28.360
Tsukushi, you can't!
What are you going to tell your mom?

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.110
Shut up, Kazuya!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.050
It's all right.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:36.900
It was wrong for an ordinary girl
like me...

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:39.550
...to enter this school, to begin with.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:41.790
Makino...

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.190
Tsukushi...

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.250
Everything will be all right
if I go, right?

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.800
That's what I'll do.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.100
<i>Again...</i>

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.710
<i>Why does he look at me like that?</i>

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:06.350
<i>Why?</i>

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.120
I won't allow Makino to be expelled.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:25.730
I caused this mess. I'll leave.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:45.550
In that case, why don't you both quit?

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.320
Tsukasa!

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:52.190
If you make Rui quit, I'll quit too.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.520
Me, too.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.060
What was that?

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.560
If Tsukushi has to quit,
then I'll quit too.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.870
I've had enough! Whatever happened
to the cool F4?

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:07.340
Yeah. Wasn't our bond 
stronger than anything?

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.940
Are you guys planning to
double-cross me?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.610
Shut up!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.590
You're a fine bunch of yammering,
sniveling so-called friends.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:17.550
I'm getting sick just listening to you.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:21.520
Why don't you use sports to
resolve your differences fairly?

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.110
S...

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:24.090
S...

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.720
Sports?

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:29.560
That's right.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:33.060
A healthy friendship will grow
from a healthy body.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.230
Form two teams of three.

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:37.240
The losers will accept
the demands of the winners.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.000
No hard feelings.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.480
A sports showdown?!

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:42.690
Among the F4?

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.780
That's so uncool!

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:49.440
That's the fairest way. Right?

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:56.050
Teams of three. Yes,
how about a three on three?

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:58.400
Three on three?

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.820
Basketball...

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:04.560
We divide up into threes and score
as many baskets as we can.

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.030
Three on three...

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.510
Okay... Let's do it.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.080
Tsukasa!

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:28.950
But if we win, you're going
to be expelled.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.590
J-just a minute... 
Three on three means...

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.840
Expelled?

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:58.210
Let's practice, since we're here.
The match is tomorrow!

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:06.260
Those three look great,
but they might not play well at all.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.320
They play well, alright.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.630
Scouts came from all over when
we were in junior high.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.890
It's not worth breaking a sweat.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.400
We know who'll win.

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:26.000
But, for him...

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.880
Shoot!

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.390
We're goners.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.330
It's an important match...

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.650
"If he leads, all will be well."

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.650
Follow his (her) lead
and all will be well.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.810
Stop standing there staring.
Let's practice.

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:17.150
I'll support you.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:32.160
I won't let them expel us.
I have something I want to protect, too.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.300
Let's go.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:46.170
Okay!

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:10.730
You let your hair down a little

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:18.600
You hid the fact
that you were crying

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:28.480
I noticed, but I
couldn't ask you why

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:36.520
I can never be
honest about how I feel

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:44.300
Until after we've split
up after a bad fight

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:52.440
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:52.440
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:22:52.440 --> 00:23:00.810
I can say "I love you"...

00:22:52.440 --> 00:23:00.810
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:10.590
Do you really hate me this time?

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:18.360
Will you end up running to him?

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:26.540
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:26.540
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:34.950
I can say "I love you"...

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:34.950
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:52.530
My heart has ricocheted between
love's joy and love's pain.

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:55.700
And Domyoji and Rui Hanazawa's
hearts clashed...

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:59.700
The match that ends it all
is about to begin.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:03.170
Next on Hana Yori Dango:
"Two Ways to Love"

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:06.210
I will follow Rui Hanazawa.

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:07.540
That's my decision.
